{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"agent_message","text":"The wider-GEMM route changes rocBLAS’s algorithm at one workload and breaks the value projection’s strict rounding there, so I’m not adopting it globally. A safer opportunity is concurrency: Q, K, and V are independent, and small/medium 1024×1024 projections do not fill all 256 compute units. I’m benchmarking the same three PyTorch GEMMs on separate GPU streams, preserving their exact outputs."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport torch,triton\nimport kernel, reference\nstreams=[torch.cuda.Stream() for _ in range(3)]\n\ndef concurrent(args):\n    x,qw,kw,vw,qn,kn,eps=args\n    cur=torch.cuda.current_stream()\n    for s in streams: s.wait_stream(cur)\n    with torch.cuda.stream(streams[0]): q=x@qw.t()\n    with torch.cuda.stream(streams[1]): k=x@kw.t()\n    with torch.cuda.stream(streams[2]): v=x@vw.t()\n    for s in streams: cur.wait_stream(s)\n    bs,sl,_=x.shape; rows=bs*sl\n    q=q.view(bs,sl,8,128);k=k.view(bs,sl,8,128);v=v.view(bs,sl,8,128)\n    qo=torch.empty_like(q);ko=torch.empty_like(k)\n    kernel._qk_rms_kernel[(triton.cdiv(rows,4),8)](q,k,qn,kn,qo,ko,rows,eps,BLOCK_M=4,num_warps=4)\n    return qo,ko,v\n\nfor m in (128,131,256,512,586,1024,2048,2164,4096,6184,8192):\n x=torch.rand((1,m,1024),device='cuda');ws=[torch.rand((1024,1024),device='cuda') for _ in range(3)];nw=[torch.rand(128,device='cuda') for _ in range(2)]; args=(x,*ws,*nw,1e-6)\n a=kernel.run(*args);b=concurrent(args);torch.cuda.synchronize()\n exact=[(u==v).float().mean().item() for u,v in zip(a,b)]\n ta=triton.testing.do_bench(lambda:kernel.run(*args),warmup=25,rep=100)\n tb=triton.testing.do_bench(lambda:concurrent(args),warmup=25,rep=100)\n print(m,f'seq {ta:.4f} conc {tb:.4f} ratio {ta/tb:.3f}',exact)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
