{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"agent_message","text":"The final layout experiment paid off: a simple Triton three-source copy concatenates the projection weights bit-for-bit in about 9.2 µs versus 14.0 µs for `torch.cat`. That saves one-third of the unavoidable packing cost and makes the wide GEMM favorable even at 2164 rows. I’m integrating it now, while retaining the exact three-GEMM fallback at 128 rows where the wide rocBLAS algorithm is numerically incompatible."}}
